WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.880
America's schools have been caught up in
a testing mania for, well, most of the 21st

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.660
century. It's long past time that we
focused on a healthier vision of good

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.560
schooling – not just reading and math, but also character, responsibility, good

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.240
citizenship. The push for social and
emotional learning – or SEL – can help with

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.289
all of this. That's why I was pleased to
see the influential Aspen Institute

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:33.030
recently released a consensus report
from its national panel on SEL. I was

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.960
less pleased to see that the consensus
was mostly banalities, and downright

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.430
disappointed to see it filled with the
ideological gobbledygook of education

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:45.300
school progressivism. Talk of character
and personal responsibility was

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.219
conspicuous in its absence. We all want
schools to be more focused on character

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:54.480
and all the needs of our kids, but real
consensus will require honoring

00:00:54.480 --> 00:01:00.030
traditional values, not just progressive
enthusiasms. If SEL winds up hijacked by

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.100
well-meaning ideologues, a promising
cause will morph into a divisive

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.180
educational culture war. What do you
think about social and emotional

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.700
What do you
think about social and emotional

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.500
learning? Let us know in your comments.
Also, let us know what other topics you'd

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.150
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,
and be sure to like and subscribe for

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:23.030
more research and videos from AEI.

